{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-MRSA, Anti-inflammatory", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Rich", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (61.54%) to synthetic W5K02 W: 33%, K: 33%, and R: 33%. Chemical modification: C-terminal amidation. Peptide engineering: this peptide consists of all D-amino acids. Activity: active against S. aureus ATCC 33591 and 6 MRSA clinical strains (MIC 8 uM) and K. pneumoniae ATCC 700603 (MIC 8 uM), K. pneumoniae 5 MDR strains (MIC 16-128 uM). Resistance development:no:bacteria:S. aureus: Resistance development:no:bacteria:K. pneumoniae: not observed after 14 passages. MOA:bacteria:S. aureus: MOA:bacteria:K. pneumoniae: permeated bacterial membranes, leadin to pore formation (ATP release) and ROS release at 2x and 4x MIC only. In vitro toxicity: human RBC, no hemolysis at 2028 uM, not hemo.lytic. Cytotoxicity: BV-2 cells (TC50 32-64 uM), murine RAW 264.7 cells (TC50 64-128 uM), and HK-2 cells (TC50 128 uM). Anti-inflammatory: suppressed the level of cytokines IL-1beta, TNF-alpha, IL-12, IL-17, IL_18, and iNOS released from LPS-treated murine RAW 264.7. In vivo toxicity:mouse: no weight loss or mouse death at 30 mg/kg (MTD) for 7 days. Animal model:mouse:pneumonia: intratracheal spraying infected lung and i.p. treatment at 4, 8, and 12 h at 5 or 10 mg/kg (dose-dependent efficacy at CFU decrease ~2 log).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "41290594", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Nat Commun. 2025 Nov 25;16(1):10488. doi: 10.1038/s41467-025-65449-w. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP06279", "source_id": "AP06279", "source_numeric_id": "06279", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP06279", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "An antimicrobial peptide as a potential therapy for bacterial pneumonia that alleviates antimicrobial resistance.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
